.ad l
.nh
.SH NAME
QVBoxLayout \- Lines up widgets vertically
.SH SYNOPSIS
.br
.PP
\fC#include <qlayout.h>\fR
.PP
Inherits QBoxLayout.
.PP
.SS "Public Members"
.in +1c
.ti -1c
.BI "\fBQVBoxLayout\fR ( QWidget * " "parent" ", int " "border" "=0, int " "space" " = -1, const char * " "name" "=0 ) "
.br
.ti -1c
.BI "\fBQVBoxLayout\fR ( QLayout * " "parentLayout" ", int " "space" " = -1, const char * " "name" "=0 ) "
.br
.ti -1c
.BI "\fBQVBoxLayout\fR ( int " "space" " = -1, const char * " "name" "=0 ) "
.br
.ti -1c
.BI "\fB~QVBoxLayout\fR () "
.br
.in -1c
.SH DESCRIPTION
The QVBoxLayout class lines up widgets vertically.
.PP
This class provides an easier way to construct vertical box layout objects. See QBoxLayout for more details.
.PP
The simplest way to use this class is:
.PP
.nf
.br
     QBoxLayout * l = new QVBoxLayout( widget );
.br
     l->addWidget( aWidget );
.br
     l->addWidget( anotherWidget );
.fi
.PP
See also QHBoxLayout, QGridLayout and Layout overview documentation
.PP
Examples:
.(l
layout/layout.cpp i18n/main.cpp scrollview/scrollview.cpp customlayout/main.cpp
.)l
.SH MEMBER FUNCTION DOCUMENTATION
.SH "QVBoxLayout::QVBoxLayout ( QLayout * parentLayout, int space = -1, const char * name=0 )"
Constructs a new vertical box and adds it to \fIparentLayout.\fR
.SH "QVBoxLayout::QVBoxLayout ( QWidget * parent, int border=0, int space = -1, const char * name=0 )"
Constructs a new top-level vertical box.
.SH "QVBoxLayout::QVBoxLayout ( int space = -1, const char * name=0 )"
Constructs a new vertical box. You have to add it to another layout.
.SH "QVBoxLayout::~QVBoxLayout ()"
Destructs this box.
